    "answer": {
      "short": "Sample answers: $\\frac12$ and $\\frac13$; $\\frac13$ and $\\frac14$; $\\frac14$ and $\\frac15$; $\\frac15$ and $\\frac16$; $\\frac16$ and $\\frac17$.\n\nUnit fractions with consecutive positive denominators have this property.",
      "worked": "Choose unit fractions with consecutive denominators and check their product and difference.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12\\times\\frac13&=\\frac16, &\\frac12-\\frac13&=\\frac{3-2}{6}=\\frac16\\\\\\frac13\\times\\frac14&=\\frac1{12}, &\\frac13-\\frac14&=\\frac{4-3}{12}=\\frac1{12}\\\\\\frac14\\times\\frac15&=\\frac1{20}, &\\frac14-\\frac15&=\\frac{5-4}{20}=\\frac1{20}\\\\\\frac15\\times\\frac16&=\\frac1{30}, &\\frac15-\\frac16&=\\frac{6-5}{30}=\\frac1{30}\\\\\\frac16\\times\\frac17&=\\frac1{42}, &\\frac16-\\frac17&=\\frac{7-6}{42}=\\frac1{42}\\end{align*}$$\nEach pair has the same product and difference.",
